Withdrawn: turn accelerated compositing off where OpenGL is a CPU rasterizer.

Against perf/home-billboard-software (it reuses that branch's renderer probe). At the start of
`run`, before Tauri creates a web view, the app probed OpenGL and, on a software rasterizer,
replaced itself with a copy started with WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1.

It does what it says: the restart happens, the web process no longer runs llvmpipe. And it
leaves the real app with a black window (shots/real-2.52.6-settle.png, against
shots/real-2.52.6-composited.png): the player's GtkGLArea puts the window on OpenGL, and GTK 3
does not draw a non-composited web view in such a window. Kept for the record.

